# A window is READONLY, so it declares no mutable walk. `iterateMut` lives on
# the owning list, where an exclusive receiver can be had.
#
# The refusal lands at EMIT rather than typecheck: a container mono is lenient
# about members it does not declare, so the undeclared call reaches the emitter
# as a binding it cannot type. The result is BOUND on purpose -- in statement
# position the same call is dropped in silence, which is a wider hole in that
# leniency than this fixture is about.
main: function is {
    ns: (ListVal i64)
    ns.append from: 1
    sl: ns.slice from: 0 to: 1
    it: sl.iterateMut
    print "unreachable"
}
